<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wagria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wagria is a historical region in eastern Holstein, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, between the Bay of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a> and the Bay of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wagri">Wagrians</a>, a West Slavic people of the Obotrite confederation whose chief centre was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/starigard">Starigard</a> (Oldenburg). Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-ii-of-holstein">Adolf II of Holstein</a> conquered it in the 1130s and 1140s, settled it with Germans, Flemings and Frisians and founded Lübeck in 1143.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wagria.jpg" alt="Wagria" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joan Blaeu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Wagrien.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
